        "mission_intent": "We need to stand up a persistent collection posture focused on PRC maritime coercion activities across the South China Sea, specifically monitoring Coast Guard and maritime militia operations near Second Thomas Shoal and adjacent disputed features in the Spratlys. Given Manila's firm stance on maintaining its outpost, the risk of inadvertent escalation is climbing and we need near-real-time indications and warning. Task the appropriate GEOINT and SIGINT assets to establish baseline patterns of life for PRC Coast Guard vessels operating in the vicinity, with particular attention to water cannon employment, use of floating barriers, and any repositioning of assets from PRC-militarized island garrisons. Coordinate with INDOPACOM J2 for deconfliction of collection windows and ensure fusion reporting is tagged for the South China Sea Escalation Watch thread. I also want a parallel collection line covering PRC naval and coast guard activity around the Senkaku Islands to identify any correlation between tempo shifts in the East and South China Seas. Reporting cadence should be daily situational updates with flash notifications for any physical contact or near-miss incidents involving Philippine or Japanese vessels. Please have the initial collection plan back to me by close of business Friday for review before we push it through the requirements management system.",
